  "findings": {
    "sui": "The unmodified 13.5.1 module is marked unloaded and its server is absent on both cores. The linker reports empty/missing DT_HASH/DT_GNU_HASH while loading its memfd library. ARM64 PT_LOAD segments have 4096-byte alignment and noncongruent 16 KiB offsets.",
    "neozygisk": "The unmodified 2.4 provider does not inject the same API v5 fixture on either core at 16 KiB; it passes at 4 KiB. Its ARM64 executable and libraries also have noncongruent 16 KiB PT_LOAD layouts.",
    "busybox": "The unmodified busybox-ndk 13614 ARM64 SELinux binary segfaults when executing true on this 16 KiB guest under both cores. Installed bytes match across controls and have noncongruent 16 KiB PT_LOAD layouts. The 4 KiB run works; this does not affect the separately qualified BusyBox bundled with Kitsune."
  },
  "limits": "These exact ZIPs fail the named 16 KiB functions. Install/removal and root recovery pass. This is not a failure of the builtin API v5 probe, Zygisk Next or ReZygisk, which pass on the same page size. Alternative-loader Sui combinations are evaluated separately.",
